# Cognito OIDC auth — all three required for auth to activate.
# If any is missing, the auth gate is open (dev/CI mode).
#
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN  — Cognito hosted UI domain (without https://)
#   e.g. "2beefarm.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com"
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID — App client ID from the Cognito User Pool
#   (must be a PUBLIC client, no secret — this is a SPA)
# VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI — Where Cognito redirects after login
#   Must match the app client's registered callback URL exactly.
#
# The app client must have:
#   - Allowed OAuth flows: Authorization code grant
#   - Allowed OAuth scopes: openid, email, profile
#   - PKCE enabled (public client)
#
# 🔴 ALL THREE OR NONE OF THEM. There is no middle state, and there used not to
# be a check: until 2026-08-27 a build with SOME of these set served the whole
# app with NO sign-in at all, silently, looking exactly like local-development
# mode. It now refuses to open and names what is missing (`authConfigState`).
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE SHIPPED A PARTIAL CONFIG. `VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI` carried a
# real value beside two blanks, so `cp .env.example .env && npm run build`
# produced a build that will not open. Blanked — the example is the state a
# developer should start from, and that state is "no auth".
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 WHICH APP CLIENT — and it is NOT the obvious one (added 2026-08-30)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The pool `two-bee-users` (ap-southeast-2_65Y4fzSoR) carries TWO app clients and
# picking the wrong one fails in the most confusing way available: the hosted UI
# loads, the login SUCCEEDS, and the auth code is then redirected to somebody
# else's callback. Nothing in the app reports it, because nothing in the app is
# involved by then.
#
#   ✅ 2bee-app-oidc                              35t0ursokc57thbfspl1jq9gu7
#        callbacks: http://localhost:5178/ , https://2bee.app/
#        flows: code (PKCE only)          <- THIS ONE
#
#   ❌ HiveUserPoolHiveAppClientF22A707C-…        3jtujit8dc1duv373d8t9opvrp
#        callback:  https://example.com   (only)
#        flows: code + implicit, scope aws.cognito.signin.user.admin
#        This is the main dashboard's client. It is not ours.
#
# ⚠ These are written down BECAUSE THE WRONG ONE WAS USED. `web/.env` carried
# the Hive client from 2026-08-21 until backend caught it on 2026-08-30 — nine
# days — and the gate looked unblocked the whole time: the client exists, OAuth
# is enabled on it, and the login screen renders. Only the round trip breaks.
#
# ⚠ A public SPA client id is NOT a secret. It is compiled into the bundle and
# served to every visitor, so recording it here costs nothing and is the only
# thing that stops the next person guessing. The values are `TwoBeeApi`'s CFN
# outputs `App2beeCognitoClientId` / `App2beeCognitoDomain` — re-derive with:
#
#   aws --profile 696 cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name TwoBeeApi \
#     --query "Stacks[0].Outputs[?contains(OutputKey,'Cognito')]"
#
# ⚠ DOMAIN TAKES NO `https://` PREFIX — `auth.ts` prepends it. A handover ticket
# once showed `VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=https://2bee-farm…`; that example was wrong.

# The redirect URI, when you do fill these in, is the app client's registered
# callback URL exactly — for the served product that is https://2bee.app/ .
